# agent-bridge per-machine env overrides — EXAMPLE
#
# Copy to ~/.config/agent-bridge/machine.env (or set AGENT_BRIDGE_MACHINE_ENV
# to another path) and uncomment the lines that apply to THIS host. The wrapper
# (scripts/wrapper/agent-bridge-wrapper.sh) sources this file before its
# always-on defaults, so values here act like per-host caller env.
#
# Convention: use `export VAR="${VAR:-value}"` guards so a true per-call
# override (`VAR=… agent-bridge …`) still wins over the per-host default.
#
# This file is per-host and must NOT be committed to the shared repo — hosts
# differ (different SKUs, paths, checkouts).

# --- Context window (forum #1758) ---
# Set ONLY on a host whose sessions run the 1M-context beta. The opus-4.x /
# sonnet-4.x model id is identical for the 200K and 1M SKUs, so the tool can't
# detect it — this is how a 1M host tells context_pressure_estimate the truth.
# A 200K host must leave this UNSET (setting it would under-report fatigue and
# risk overrunning the real window).
#
# export AGENT_BRIDGE_CONTEXT_WINDOW="${AGENT_BRIDGE_CONTEXT_WINDOW:-1000000}"
